# Which libchdr the folder libchdr/ beside this file is a copy of: the branch,
# the commit it is in upstream's repository (github.com/rtissera/libchdr, the
# master of 2026-10-11), and every file of that commit's tree with the id git
# gives its content there. Any checkout of upstream prints the same list with
# `git ls-tree -r <commit>`, so the copy can be held against it without a file
# being fetched. The one release upstream has tagged, v0.3.0, is 118 commits
# older and lacks the fixes a file made to mislead the reader is met with, so
# the copy is of a commit and not of a release.
#
# The copy is 48 files of that tree as upstream has them, byte for byte: there
# is no `patch` line here and no folder of patches, and a file that is not
# upstream's is a file to take again. With libchdr come the decompressors it
# carries in deps/ and include/dr_libs: the LZMA SDK's decoder, miniz, the one
# file Zstandard's decoder is distributed as, and dr_flac.
#
# The other 83 files of the tree are left out on purpose, each on a line that
# says `left-out` where the others say `file`, and such a file has to be
# absent: upstream's workflows, its CMake files and the ones in deps/, its
# tests and their corpora, the ports to boards in contrib/ and cmake/, the
# notes in docs/, the assembler of the LZMA decoder, a second FLAC decoder
# written in C++, and unity.c, link.T and pkg-config.pc.in, which belong to
# upstream's own build, by which nothing here is built.
#
# Two licence texts are not in upstream's tree, which carries miniz and
# Zstandard without them. They are kept in licenses/ beside this file, each
# on a `licence` line with the id git gives its content in the repository it
# was taken from:
#   miniz-3.1.2-LICENSE   github.com/richgel999/miniz, tag 3.1.2,
#                         commit 77d0dce8627735138c51770d1799a1ef48f2117d,
#                         the file LICENSE
#   zstd-1.5.7-LICENSE    github.com/facebook/zstd, tag v1.5.7,
#                         commit f8745da6ff1ad1e7bab384bd1f9d742439278e99,
#                         the file LICENSE
#
# shared/tests/vendored_check.py holds the folder and the two texts to all of
# this. To take a later libchdr: copy the files wanted from a checkout of the
# new commit, with `git add -f` since the tree may carry a .gitignore; write
# the `upstream` line with the commit, and one line for every file that
# `git ls-tree -r <commit>` prints, `file` for those copied and `left-out`
# for the rest; take the licence text of a dependency whose version changed
# from that version's tag and rename it.
